I'm also not clear as to how you would compare error model fits in the situation where you assign the uere value directly.

So say I took my stationary data and did the following...

data$HDOP <- sqrt(2 * data$pred.error)
uere(data) <- 1

How would I compare this model to one where I ran uere.fit(data) using that HDOP column? Directly assigning the uere to 1 doesn't produce a Z^2 or AIC estimate so I'm not sure how to make a comparison of this error model to another.
Normally I make these model comparisons on the stationary data first but ran into that hiccup.

